From baafcb400415434db490a1b725bbb85483126cd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 03:46:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel interfaces built on the generic interfaces,
 generic_functions option

- material properties: the code evaluating a material property at a point
  (order of the checks, policies, bounds macro, body) is written once by
  `GenericMaterialPropertyInterfaceBase::writePointEvaluation`, the
  reporting of the checks being given by the caller: the `generic` and
  `cyrano` interfaces keep their messages, the kernels of the
  `generic-parallel` interface report the identifiers of the checks, now
  given by the base. `GenericParallelMaterialPropertyInterface` derives from
  `GenericMaterialPropertyInterfaceBase`. The function of a point of the
  `generic` interface is written by `writePointwiseFunction`, whose names
  and types are given explicitly.
- models: `GenericParallelModelInterface` derives from
  `GenericModelInterface`, which is no longer final.
- behaviours: the functions of the `generic` interface are written by
  `GenericBehaviourInterface::writeGenericFunctions`, whose options select
  the files, the symbols and the linkage of the out of bounds policy; the
  behaviour class may hold the constructors of other interfaces
  (`AbstractBehaviourInterface::getInterfacesOfAdditionalBehaviourConstructors`).
- `generic_functions` option of the `generic-parallel` interfaces: the
  library also contains the functions of the `generic` interface and
  exports `Generic` as interface, with one set of parameters and one out
  of bounds policy shared by all its functions. The function of a point of
  a material property or of a behaviour is written in a separate source,
  compiled by the C++ compiler of the configuration; the one of a model in
  the source of the functions of batches of points.
- tests: `check-generic-functions.sh` (material properties, behaviours,
  models) called by all the configurations, `--generic-functions=true`
  option of both comparison programs; documentation.

The sources generated by the `generic` interface for behaviours and models
are unchanged; the material properties of the `generic` and `cyrano`
interfaces give the same statuses, messages and values (differential test
of the libraries generated before and after this change).
